      "title": "AFV questions (stun effect, etc.)",
      "query": "AFV questions (stun effect, etc.): Background:  I have been playing Up Front for over 40 years, but I never liked AFV's and so avoided them.  Now I'm trying to use them more, and this has raised some questions that I didn't have to think about before.\n\nIs a stunned, non-OT AFV forced to button up?  I think I had always assumed the answer was \"yes\", but re-reading the rules yesterday, I wasn't sure.  The clearest rule I can find is 28.45, which says, \"A stun result flips any CE AFV card over to its Pinned/Button Up side.\"\n\nWell, that is ambiguous.  It says it's only referring to CE AFVs, but then it mentions a Buttoned Up side, which a CE AFV does not have.  I think on the whole that I would find it odd that regular AFV's don't button up when stunned when OT AFV's do, but that's not much of a guide to go on.\n\nI'd like to follow this up with a dumb question about boxed attacks.  I'm pretty sure I understand them, but they seem weird, so I just wanted to verify.  In brief:  when you shoot a boxed effect number against an AFV, you know exactly what's going to happen if you hit.  You simply add your boxed number to your relative range, and compare that to the defending AFV's numbers.  (There are exceptions for rifleman using inherent boxed FP at range 5 and for LATW.)  This feels weird to me because everything else in Up Front is accompanied by massive amounts of randomness, so for a hit's result to be absolutely known (with the possible exception of an immobilization or stun in case they have the same effect number) seems incongruous.  I just want to make sure I'm getting it right.",
      "intent": "clarification",
      "expected_rules": [
        "25.4",
        "26.5",
        "28.3",
        "28.43",
        "28.431",
        "28.45",
        "6.5"
      ],
      "retrieved_rules": [],
