      "ground_truth_answer": "I think I understand the infiltration and the CC rules but one sentence has me puzzled under 20.73: \"However, if he already has infiltrator status he may keep it to use in any subsequent CC or normal Fire attack against the infiltrated group only if he has defeated his last CC opponent by 3 or more in the resolution of their CC\".\n\nThe bolded part is mine and is the one that is confusing me. I didn't see a situation where a CC attacker would not be infiltrated?\n\nYou are correct, the attacker man in CC will be an infiltrator.  As pointed out above, a man in the defending group could be infiltrating the attacking group (or a different attacking group also at RR5), and rule covers those situations.  \n\nNote, it is more difficult to infiltrate from a group which has been infiltrated by their opponent (20.39)\n\nThere might be others, but what pops to mind is 20.9 Berserk, and (although it was likely not considered when 20.73 was written), 45.4 BANZAI.\n\nKeeping infiltration status would not apply to Banzai or Berserk, because in neither case is the man an infiltrator.  (20.91, 45.422)",
